// Package ffi holds the Go bindings to the zeclib Rust backend.
//
// ffi.go and ffi.h are generated by uniffi-bindgen-go from the compiled Rust
// crate in ../../rust and are not edited by hand. ../../build.sh regenerates
// them. The bindings are only compiled with the "zec" build tag and cgo, and
// they link the static library that build.sh stages under ../../lib.
//
// The generated API is not used directly outside package zeclib. It panics
// when an object is used after Destroy, reports optional values as pointers,
// and returns errors whose text is generated. Package zeclib wraps it in an
// API that does none of these.
package ffi
